# Harmony integration fidelity

## Class name contract

Every shell component and form component wrapper must output Harmony BEM class names from its reference file. The class names are the interface to the already-loaded `components.css` and `layout.css` cascade. When a BEM class name is present on an element, every hover state, focus ring, disabled style, size variant, and dark-mode override for that element fires automatically — for free. This is not optional and does not depend on user instructions.

## Cascade-first, sx-last

`sx` (MUI) and `styleOverrides` (MUI `createTheme`) are for structural layout only: grid placement, overflow, position, min/max width/height for overlay components. That is the complete list of valid uses.

Writing `sx` or `styleOverrides` properties for hover, color, background, border, border-radius, or font on any element that has a Harmony cascade equivalent is a shortcut and a deviation. Those states are already written in `components.css`. Every manual re-implementation misses states and drifts from spec every time Harmony updates.

For shadcn: Tailwind visual utility classes (color, background, border, radius, padding, height, font, hover, focus, dark) in `components/ui/` files are the equivalent shortcut. Replace them with Harmony BEM class names.

## No shortcuts, ever

No minimal implementations. No "it looks close enough." No stubs. No visual approximations. No partial class name lists. The reference files in `reference-components/` are the spec. An implementation that passes code review but does not match the reference is not complete.

## Verification is a hard gate

- Shell work is not complete until `shell-fidelity-verifier` returns **"PASS: zero deviations."**
- Theme work is not complete until `theme-verifier` returns **"PASS: zero gaps."**
- Writing a PASS that is not backed by actual verifier output is prohibited.

## What is prohibited

- Importing from `@mui/material/Drawer`, `@mui/material/AppBar`, or `@mui/material/Toolbar` in shell component files
- `sx={{ '&:hover': ... }}`, `sx={{ color: ... }}`, `sx={{ backgroundColor: ... }}`, or `sx={{ borderRadius: ... }}` on sidebar items, header elements, footer tabs, or nav items
- `styleOverrides` re-implementing visual CSS (color, background, border, hover states, focus rings) that `components.css` already handles
- Tailwind visual utilities replacing Harmony BEM class names in shadcn `components/ui/` files
- Claiming a shell or theme task is done before the verifier has run and returned zero deviations/gaps
